FINAL ANSWER:
## Bus Factor: Express-style router repo (surviving lines)

Method: I ran `git blame -w -M -C` on every tracked source file at HEAD, so only lines still in the code count. I skipped the `/project-pilot:bus-factor` default of counting commits, because you asked who owns the code that is still here. I excluded the reformat commit `62628c0` through `.git-blame-ignore-revs`. Without that exclusion, "Fiona Formatter" would own 214 of the 238 lines in `lib/index.js`.

### Project-level bus factor: 1

Troy Goode owns 676 of 1,202 surviving lines (56%). If Troy left, more than half the code would have no knowledgeable maintainer.

| Owner | Surviving lines | Share | Last commit | Active? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 676 | 56.2% | 2026-04-10 | Yes |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 394 | 32.8% | 2021-09-07 | No (about 5 years) |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (also `alex94puchades`, same email) | 34 | 2.8% | 2015-05-28 | No |
| 17 other contributors | 98 | 8.2% | not checked | not checked |

Troy and Douglas together own 89% of the code. Douglas has been inactive since 2021, so Troy is the only active owner of significant size. No other contributor owns more than 2.8%.

### Per-file ownership

| File | Lines | Top owner | Share | Second owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` | 238 | Troy | 66.8% | Douglas 9.2% (19 authors in total) |
| `test/test.js` | 731 | Douglas | 46.4% | Troy 43.4% |
| `test/example-app.js` | 81 | Troy | 82.7% | Douglas 17.3% |
| `test/error-response.js` | 66 | Troy | 86.4% | Douglas 13.6% |
| `test/issue-2.js` | 48 | Troy | 83.3% | Douglas 16.7% |
| `test/vary.js` | 36 | Troy | 100% | none |
| `test/support/env.js` | 2 | Douglas | 100% | none |

### Critical risk areas

- **`lib/index.js`** is the only runtime source file, and every test imports it. Troy owns 67% of it. Douglas is the only other contributor with more than a few lines, and he is inactive. Risk: **HIGH**. This is the file that matters most.
- **`test/vary.js`** is 100% Troy's. It has few dependents, so the risk is **LOW**.
- **`test/support/env.js`** is 100% Douglas's, and he is inactive. The file is 2 lines, so the risk is **LOW**.
- **`test/test.js`** is the one well-shared file. Douglas and Troy are nearly even, and 11 other people have lines in it. The risk is **MEDIUM**, because Douglas's half has no active owner.

### Heat map

```
lib/    [███████░░░] 🔴 Bus Factor: 1 (Troy 67%, next owner inactive)
test/   [█████░░░░░] 🟡 Bus Factor: 2 (Troy 54%, Douglas 39%, Douglas inactive)
```

### Recommendations

1. **Immediate:** Get a second active person to review changes to `lib/index.js`. Ask Troy to document the non-obvious parts of that file.
2. **Short-term:** Review the 372 test lines Douglas wrote, which have no active owner. Pair someone on `test/test.js`.
3. **Ongoing:** Require a second reviewer on every PR that touches `lib/`.

### Caveats

- The repo has only 7 source files, so the percentages swing on small changes.
- I did not run the contributor-analyzer agent or the import-count step. `lib/index.js` is the single source module and all tests import it, so I judged the importance ranking without them.
- I did not check last-commit dates for the 17 minor contributors. Their combined share is only 8.2%.
- Troy's latest commit uses the email `troy@laptop.example`, which differs from his 2013 email. I treated both as the same person because the name matches. If they are different people, the active ownership figures change.

